{#
  How one format runs across the machines a scenario names: a subsection after the single-host instructions rather than
  a rewrite of them, because most of what those say -- building the images, loading the credential, opening the UIs --
  holds on the server machine unchanged. What differs is which machine starts what.
#}
{% from "readme/commands.j2" import process_compose_up %}
{% set server = section.machines | first %}
### Run Across Machines With {{ section.heading }}

{% if section.format == "dekit" %}
Copy this directory to each machine and start that machine's share there. Every task is tagged
with its machine and none starts on `dekit up` alone, so `dekit up` on any machine starts nothing
until its tag is started.
{% elif section.format == "process-compose" %}
Copy this directory to each machine and start only that machine's namespace there.
{% elif section.format == "docker-compose" %}
Copy this directory to each machine and start only that machine's profile there.
{% else %}
Copy this directory to each machine and start that machine's share of the scenario there.
{% endif %}
{% if server.board %}
`{{ server.name }}` is a {{ server.board }} running `ws-server` as firmware,
and the runners on every other machine reach the hub at `{{ server.address }}`, which the network the board
joins has to resolve to it. Its share is loading the firmware, which it then runs from power-on.
{% elif shares_hubs %}
`{{ server.name }}` runs OpenObserve, `ws-server`, and the NATS server and object store the hubs share,
which the other machines' hubs reach at `{{ server.address }}`. Each runner joins the hub on its own
machine, or the one on `{{ server.name }}` when its machine runs none.
{% else %}
`{{ server.name }}` runs OpenObserve and `ws-server`, and the runners on every other machine reach
the hub at `{{ server.address }}`.
{% endif %}

{% include "readme/loopback.md.j2" %}
{% for machine in section.machines %}
On `{{ machine.name }}`:

```bash
{# A board's share is its firmware, which every format loads the same way. #}
{%     if machine.board %}
mise run {{ machine.flash }}
{%     elif section.format == "dekit" %}
dekit up
dekit start +{{ machine.name }}
{%     elif section.format == "process-compose" %}
{{ process_compose_up }} -n {{ machine.name }}
{%     elif section.format == "docker-compose" %}
docker compose --profile {{ machine.name }} up --build
{%     else %}
mise run {{ machine.task }}
{%     endif %}
```
{%     if not loop.last %}

{%     endif %}
{% endfor %}
